{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404246-how-would-your-pcs-handle-this-scenario","id":1404246,"title":"How would your PCs handle this scenario?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-23T09:34:48-07:00","id":1404246,"title":"How would your PCs handle this scenario?","content":"My players are doing a favor for Trisenji Yilean - the criminal No Moon operating in Varangia. The group is mostly oriented toward stealth and subterfuge. All but one of the characters (the Full Moon) has a few dots of Stealth and Larceny - they're a Changing Moon smuggler, a No Moon gambling sorcerer, a Casteless cat burglar, and a Twilight doctor / poisoner. The Full Moon is a bounty hunter / tracker with a lot of pets. The Lunar can all move freely in the city since they can disguise themselves as locals; the Twilight will have a harder time with disguising himself and is currently stuck in the foreign quarter.<br /> <br /> Trisenji wants them to fudge the numbers on the impending birth of a wazir's child. If the child is born after midnight tomorrow, then the kid will be put into the pandit caste. If the kid is born slightly before midnight, they'll end up in the water-carrier caste instead. Trisenji wants the records to show that the kid was born before midnight and has tasked the group with tampering with the five clocks and watches that will be used to record the time of birth. These belong to the pregnant wazir herself, her husband (a notorious gambler), the physician currently administering drugs to delay the birth, the pandit performing on-the-spot astrological readings for the birth, and the the clock in the house. Trisenji himself is taking care of the clock tower in the center of town. Trisenji advised them that the expectant parents will want at least 3 timepieces to verify the birth, so 2 of the five can just go missing or be destroyed - though he recommends against that since it might call too much attention to their efforts. The time pieces will also be checked against the clock tower at sunset, so any tampering has to be done after that. They considered just changing the clock tower, but were told that the if clock tower disagrees with the clocks in the manors of the five local wazirs then they'll also know something is up.<br /> <br /> The Casteless' player looked at me like I was crazy when I gave them this scenario, and we ended the session then to give the players some time to plan their heist(s). They all seemed to be at a loss on how to tackle this.<br /> <br /> So how would your PCs do it? Or how would you do it, if you were playing these characters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T10:11:25-07:00","id":1404251,"title":"","content":"Forget the clocks. Tamper with the drugs delaying the birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T10:19:33-07:00","id":1404255,"title":"","content":"My players would cut the Gordian Knot.<br /> <br /> The Twilight crafts birth inducing drugs.<br /> Any one of the Lunars performs the sacred hunt on the physician giving the birth delaying drugs and administers the Solar Crafted birth inducing drugs.<br /> The kid pops out on the spot and is born well before midnight.<br /> <br /> I, a murderhobo, would leave nothing to chance and have the Lunars Hunt everyone involved. Husband, physician, pandit. Heck, hunt Trisenji as well, just in case.<br /> <br /> Were it important that the kid is actually born a pandit... any of the Halloween episodes of Brooklyn 99 are good inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-23-2020, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T10:20:41-07:00","id":1404257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404246-how-would-your-pcs-handle-this-scenario?p=1404251#post1404251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forget the clocks. Tamper with the drugs delaying the birth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely an option they've discussed. The Twilight wanted to induce labor, but the hurdle here is that the other physician is already administering drugs to postpone labor. So he has to balance out whatever is already being used, potentially without being in the room if he has to brew up the drugs and have someone else deliver them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T10:36:19-07:00","id":1404260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404246-how-would-your-pcs-handle-this-scenario?p=1404255#post1404255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My players would cut the Gordian Knot.<br /> <br /> The Twilight crafts birth inducing drugs.<br /> Any one of the Lunars performs the sacred hunt on the physician giving the birth delaying drugs and administers the Solar Crafted birth inducing drugs.<br /> The kid pops out on the spot and is born well before midnight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm honestly expecting some sacred hunts, especially since they have several alternative means of gaining forms (the bounty hunter can incapacitate for a form, the smuggler can seduce people for their forms, the gambler can wager for a form, and the thief can burgle for a form). I think they're a little hesitant on this front though because 1) they don't want to leave too many witnesses / a trail of bodies that could reveal their schemes, and 2) getting the medicine roll right for administering the drugs could be very tricky for them since only the Twilight has Medicine. The No Moon could probably do it with an Intelligence excellency, but he's also the least likely to put himself front and center for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2118-reminiscent-oasis","name":"Reminiscent Oasis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2118_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"158"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T11:10:55-07:00","id":1404264,"title":"","content":"Let's see if I got this right.<br /> <br /> The circle's goal is to guarantee the kid is born a bit before midnight, and the family in question is doing all it can to delay to after midnight?<br /> <br /> Hmmm.<br /> (night caste spymaster) would just tamper the drugs to force an early birth instead of delaying it. If she has but a few hours she can see what they look like, commission a same-looking variant that induces birth and replace it. If it's really urgent she's good enough she can replace them as they are about to be applied and even a paranoid dragon-blood won't be able to tell.<br /> <br /> (battles caste witcher) can probably perform a similar tampering as the spymaster, and he can rig the medicine himself and events would conspire to keep detractors and investigators away. <br /> <br /> (dawn caste professor-swordsman) would grind the astrologer's nose with a lecture on how bullshit his readings are, and show a correct reading that puts the kid in the water-carrier caste even if it is born later.<br /> <br /> (dawn caste sword muse) would either get half the room to hopelessly fall in love with her and promise her to lie about this or provide excellently aggressive distractions while the rest of the group tampers with any leftover evidence. By fire, song or riot she can also be distracting enough for everyone to not notice the tower clock was tampered for the whole day. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T11:21:39-07:00","id":1404265,"title":"","content":"My players would attempt a con where they convince everyone that the birth-giver is in mortal medical danger and only their Solar physician can prevent her imminent doom.<br /> <br /> It would start small, then escalate with more and more made up rituals until they manage to convince everyone that the physician must be alone with her RIGHT NOW. Then the Solar would simply counteract the birth delaying drugs during these few seconds, as well as neutralize the potency of any drugs yet to be administered.<br /> <br /> After which they declare the patient saved from certain doom, wish the whole lot luck and leave, so that they are completely out of the picture when the actual birth occurs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 07-23-2020, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T11:24:54-07:00","id":1404266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They considered just changing the clock tower, but were told that the if clock tower disagrees with the clocks in the manors of the five local wazirs then they'll also know something is up. </div> </div> </div>Then the wazirs just need not notice.<br /> (eclipse caste librarian) &lt;starts a speech to gather a crowd near their territories and summons a magma kraken&gt;<br /> <br /> Hells, later she can spin tall tales about how a passing anathema was a bad omen cursing that birth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 07-23-2020, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T13:23:34-07:00","id":1404294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reminiscent Oasis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404246-how-would-your-pcs-handle-this-scenario?p=1404257#post1404257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's definitely an option they've discussed. The Twilight wanted to induce labor, but the hurdle here is that the other physician is already administering drugs to postpone labor. So he has to balance out whatever is already being used, potentially without being in the room if he has to brew up the drugs and have someone else deliver them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a similar idea but a different approach, convince her that the drugs the physician gave her present an immediate risk to her health and that of her child. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T13:33:41-07:00","id":1404296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404246-how-would-your-pcs-handle-this-scenario?p=1404294#post1404294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I had a similar idea but a different approach, convince her that the drugs the physician gave her present an immediate risk to her health and that of her child.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming she's a mortal, this is actually probably true.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T13:41:58-07:00","id":1404298,"title":"","content":"That's what makes it such an elegant solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T14:42:29-07:00","id":1404306,"title":"","content":"There may also be divinities associated with childbirth or something that may be persuaded to get the labor train launched for early arrival. With the advantage that as a supernatural method this may also bypass the drugs and a god might be able to do so whilst immaterial and thus not at risk for discovery or interference like parts of the party are.<br /> <br /> Now away from the method of just making the birth happen early, I do have a question. Aside from the clock tower ,as that has been listed as not the job of the players, do we know how these time pieces work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T16:26:13-07:00","id":1404316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404246-how-would-your-pcs-handle-this-scenario?p=1404306#post1404306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do we know how these time pieces work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Varangian timepieces are intricate clockworks in 2E. I don't believe they've been detailed in 3E -- just &quot;mechanical&quot; in WFHW:<br /> <br /> &quot;It was an honest place, with its functional chaises, its austere writing desk, and, of course, its mechanical clock. The clock was a Varangian import that had been in this study when Swift married into the Tereya family, and it had faithfully ticked across the decades since.&quot;<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's clockwork. From The Realm:<br /> <br /> &quot;Varangian clockworks are replicated in the workshops of Juche and the Imperial city.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-23-2020, 07:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T17:41:02-07:00","id":1404324,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1184\" data-vbnamecard=\"1184\">LadyLens</a> I totally agree with this suggestion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T18:21:33-07:00","id":1404333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404246-how-would-your-pcs-handle-this-scenario?p=1404316#post1404316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Varangian timepieces are intricate clockworks in 2E. I don't believe they've been detailed in 3E -- just &quot;mechanical&quot; in WFHW:<br /> <br /> &quot;It was an honest place, with its functional chaises, its austere writing desk, and, of course, its mechanical clock. The clock was a Varangian import that had been in this study when Swift married into the Tereya family, and it had faithfully ticked across the decades since.&quot;<br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Yeah, it's clockwork. From The Realm:<br /> <br /> &quot;Varangian clockworks are replicated in the workshops of Juche and the Imperial city.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay then the tricky part will be that they need to agree to a time for setting the time pieces to in advanced. While you might be able to get away with a minor variant too wildly and it just makes the tampering obvious and gives grounds for them to just force the declaration of time of birth to be the way they want it. IE if the birth happens at 11:55, and the confirming time pieces read 11:45, 11:46, and 11:44 can easily be written off as error by those setting them. Less so if the 11:55 birth has confirming times at 11:30, 11, and 9:15.<br /> <br /> Oh possible option, disturbing as all get out, but kind of horrifically viable. What about a Caesarean? Like if you can fake a scenario where they elect for it feels like the best option, but there is a rather horrifying option of doing it anyway. Granted this would very much be a going loud scenario because the only way you're making that look even remotely natural or unsuspicious would be to drug everyone else involved so hard they're convinced their home was devoured by the Wyld and they were tormented by Rhakasha.<br /> <br /> There's also the possibility of only faking two of the time pieces. The doctor who would be handling labour, and the mother herself. Get them thinking its later on in the night and they'll have fewer problems allowing the birth to happen. The most obvious advantage would be that any drugs being used would probably be stopped once they believe its past midnight. Making it easier to slip in the labour inducing drugs and system cleanses as the medic of the group feels is needed for the desired results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T21:38:01-07:00","id":1404358,"title":"","content":"Tampering a bunch of clocks at once is definitely high up on the &quot;too difficult&quot; line of work. Your best shot would be having multiple people able to interfere with it at an appointed time, and that appointed time being guaranteed everyone can do their magic.<br /> <br /> Which...is not going to be easy either. Causing major alarm outside is one of the ways to do it. Doing it subtly and remotely? Much harder. &quot;Make sure everyone counts exactly 1517 seconds from operation start and set the clocks then.&quot; harder (this is right up the area where I would, like, ask everyone in sync to roll a difficulty 7 int + lore/war/larceny test while doing everything as if flurrying because of the split concentration). That or going for the arcane wonky sorcerous / crafting shenanigans to bridge those difficulties.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 07-24-2020, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T05:16:58-07:00","id":1404384,"title":"","content":"Pickpocketting 5 watches, winding them, then reverse pickpocketting back isn't THAT hard. You can do that on an Excellency vs mortals.<br /> <br /> The problem is that we're trying to get them to use their watches to time when to start the birth (possibly getting them to start it too early) then winding the watches back as they're using them to verify the birth so the watches say the birth was too early.<br /> <br /> Which is trivial if you are an Essence 2 Solar with Stealing From Plain Sight Spirit. Otherwise, it's quite the challenge.<br /> <br /> In Brooklyn 99 they have incredibly elaborate distractions requiring months of prep time. But they still do it with regular mortals, no powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=52T4dl8oNFo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=52T4dl8oNFo\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=52T4dl8oNFo\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=52T4dl8oNFo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T11:05:27-07:00","id":1404430,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the difficulty as I worded them is not in the tampering in itself at all, the struggle is all in the coordination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T14:17:57-07:00","id":1404453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404246-how-would-your-pcs-handle-this-scenario?p=1404430#post1404430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the difficulty as I worded them is not in the tampering in itself at all, the struggle is all in the coordination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh.<br /> <br /> All the watches, pressumably, start at the same time. Winding them back all half an hour doesn't take the second counting precision your post seemed to imply. They don't even neccessarily have to be tampered with at the same time. So long as you change the time by the same amount and no-one compares time between tamperings.<br /> <br /> The difficulty, as I see it, is that they won't start the birth until midnight (depending on how reliable these birth delaying drugs are and exactly how far along the mother is). Which means they're going to be checking their watches for the time.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's midnight! Start the birth!&quot;<br /> *three hours later*<br /> &quot;It's a boy! The time is 23:35... wait, wut?&quot;<br /> <br /> The PCs need to force the issue of the birth so it's a &quot;countdown to doom&quot; scenario. Which might be how the chips would naturally fall (the baby comes when it comes) but the PCs are invested in a particular outcome. Like, unless the woman started going into labour already, it seems plausible that the kid might not even be born for a couple of days. And, sure, you could wind everyone's clocks back an hour to stack the deck... but inducing labour seems a more straightforward option.<br /> <br /> (I agree about the usefulness of a colossal distraction.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 07-25-2020, 03:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T14:39:11-07:00","id":1404459,"title":"","content":"Now my players would likely not have any relevant skills for the job but they would likely do something very very bad say extort gods or call up demons who simply break all the clocks, rewrite the memories of everyone involved or simply see to that there are no witnesses to the birth and write whatever they like in the birth certificate or when they impersonate whoever makes the astrologic reading. Possibly bargain with dark powers for midnight to last until the birth regardless of when it comes, should certainly be some demon or other creature that can fix that.<br /> <br /> But some of those might be hard to accomplish without some charms or sorcery, but Exalts shouldn't really do it the boring nearly mundane way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","user":"chance","date":". 07-24-2020, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","name":"chance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-24T15:03:03-07:00","id":1404461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404246-how-would-your-pcs-handle-this-scenario?p=1404453#post1404453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh.<br /> <br /> All the watches, pressumably, start at the same time. Winding them back all half an hour doesn't take the second counting precision your post seemed to imply. They don't even neccessarily have to be tampered with at the same time. So long as you change the time by the same amount and no-one compares time between tamperings.</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP left the impression these guys would take their synchronicity very seriously, probably to the minute.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T00:14:35-07:00","id":1404534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1404246-how-would-your-pcs-handle-this-scenario?p=1404461#post1404461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OP left the impression these guys would take their synchronicity very seriously, probably to the minute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. But they're specifically synching with the clock tower at a set time.<br /> <br /> Even if they're corroborating that every fifteen minutes, that's still a fifteen minute window in which to work.<br /> <br /> I don't see all five of them staring constantly at their watches shouting out every minute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T04:25:58-07:00","id":1404565,"title":"","content":"It would happen during the birth itself, that's when they will all look at the same time. <br /> <br /> If the difference is noticeable there's a fairly good chance they'll simply lie, especially if the timing puts one or two on the &quot;almost&quot; threshold. <br /> <br /> Granted, you can persuade them out of the lie, but I doubt that will be easy, risk free, or enough for the job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}